# The NVDA controller client this release bundles.
#
# The mod has always spoken through NVDA - windows_nvda.c loads
# nvdaControllerClient.dll at runtime and calls it if NVDA is running -
# but the DLL is shipped by NV Access separately from NVDA itself, so
# every player had to go and find it. Several never did, and the ones
# who search for a DLL by name land on sites that serve trojans. For a
# screen reader user that is the worst possible outcome, so the file
# comes in the archive now.
#
# It is NV Access's binary, under the LGPL v2.1, redistributed
# unmodified. The mod loads it with LoadLibrary rather than linking it,
# which is the least entangled way to use it, and the licence text that
# NV Access ships inside their own zip is packed beside it.
#
# Pinned by checksum rather than "whatever is current": a release has to
# be reproducible, and an archive whose contents move under it would
# break the checksum published with it. Bumping the version here is a
# reviewable diff, which is the point.
#
# HOW TO PIN, when this file says UNPINNED or the version is bumped:
#   1. Push the change. The "NVDA controller client" CI job downloads the
#      zip, prints the URL it came from, the zip's SHA256, the archive
#      listing and the SHA256 of each DLL inside.
#   2. Copy those values in here.
#   3. Push again. The same job is now a guard: it fails if any of them
#      ever stops matching.
# A release cannot be cut while this file is UNPINNED - build-release.sh
# refuses - so an unverified binary cannot reach a player by accident.

NVDA_VERSION=2026.1.1

# Established by the CI job on 23 September 2026, from
#   https://download.nvaccess.org/releases/2026.1.1/nvda_2026.1.1_controllerClient.zip
# The archive also carries arm64 and arm64ec builds; they are not packed,
# because the mod itself ships only x86 and x64 libraries and a client
# nothing can load is just weight in the download.
#
# sha256 of the downloaded controllerClient zip
NVDA_ZIP_SHA256=2a3a70f729be0c48120c5f24a81653202827c40a7986e289ffe2275a2b45011f

# sha256 of the two DLLs inside it
NVDA_DLL_X64_SHA256=2fe60cf00be929aae32e95c1e1507a20ada4902c8fec273b3cc2d3bf5472932a
NVDA_DLL_X86_SHA256=ab824a1126fef9135f5e7fedc4ddeb8ebce73a5bfcb6086e1799971d92dca8b4
